  <div class="faq-list">
    <details class="faq-item reveal"><summary>How much does a service at Dream Haus cost?</summary><div class="faq-content">Pricing varies by stylist tier — Silver Star, Gold Star, Platinum, and Diamond. Blow dries start at $35 (Silver Star) and go up to $65 (Diamond). Women's haircuts (which include a blowout) start at $55. Full balayage starts at $295 and ranges up to $500. Hand-tied weft installs start at $300 per pack. Full pricing is on our <a href="#services" style="color:var(--hot-pink)">services menu</a>. New blonding and extension clients are required to book a consultation first.</div></details>
    <details class="faq-item reveal"><summary>How do I book an appointment?</summary><div class="faq-content">All appointments are booked by text — just send a message to <a href="sms:7324966675" style="color:var(--hot-pink);font-weight:700">(732) 496-6675</a> with the service you're interested in and your preferred dates. You can also DM us on Instagram <a href="https://www.instagram.com/dreamhaushairboutique_/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--hot-pink)">@dreamhaushairboutique_</a>. If you'd rather call, you can reach us at <a href="tel:8482177681" style="color:var(--hot-pink);font-weight:700">(848) 217-7681</a> — but text is the fastest way to get on the books. We don't accept appointment requests by email. New color and extension clients are required to book a consultation first so we can match you to the right stylist tier.</div></details>
    <details class="faq-item reveal"><summary>Is a deposit required when I book?</summary><div class="faq-content">Yes — a non-refundable deposit secures your appointment and is applied toward your service total. Extension services require a larger deposit since hair is custom-ordered for each guest.</div></details>
    <details class="faq-item reveal"><summary>What's your cancellation policy?</summary><div class="faq-content">We require <strong>48 hours' notice</strong> to cancel or reschedule. Cancellations within 48 hours forfeit the deposit. No-shows are charged 100% of the scheduled service. We send confirmation texts and reminder emails so you have plenty of time to adjust.</div></details>
    <details class="faq-item reveal"><summary>What kind of extensions do you offer?</summary><div class="faq-content">We specialize in hand-tied weft extensions and tape-ins, primarily using Bellami Hair. Hand-tied wefts are best for clients who want long-term length and volume with seamless blending and minimal damage. Tape-ins are a great entry-level option. Every extension service starts with a complimentary consultation to match color, assess your natural hair, and discuss maintenance. Most clients return every 6 to 8 weeks for a move-up.</div></details>
    <details class="faq-item reveal"><summary>Do you offer bridal services?</summary><div class="faq-content">Yes — bridal is one of our favorite things. We offer hair and makeup for brides, bridesmaids, and flower girls. Bridal hair styling starts at $350 (upstyle) and Hollywood Waves are $500. Bridal makeup is $300 with lashes included. Bridesmaid makeup is $150 and flower girls are $50. Trials start at $250 and we recommend booking your trial 1–2 months before your wedding date.</div></details>
    <details class="faq-item reveal"><summary>Do you accept walk-ins?</summary><div class="faq-content">Dream Haus is by appointment only. We're a small, intimate boutique and every guest gets dedicated chair time — that means we don't take walk-ins, but we always do our best to fit emergencies in. Text us if you're in a pinch.</div></details>
    <details class="faq-item reveal"><summary>Where are you located?</summary><div class="faq-content">We're at <strong>4070 Asbury Avenue, Tinton Falls, NJ 07753</strong>. Free parking onsite. We serve clients across all of New Jersey — including Monmouth County, the Jersey Shore (Asbury Park, Red Bank, Long Branch, Holmdel, Middletown, Manasquan, Spring Lake), Northern Jersey, and beyond. Many of our clients travel from New York City for their appointments. We're roughly 60 minutes from Lower Manhattan and 90 minutes from Brooklyn.</div></details>
